<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Paul Hasluck</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1905">1905</a>–<a href="/years/1993">1993</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Paul Hasluck was an Australian politician, historian and diplomat. As minister for territories from 1951 to 1963 he directed policy in Papua and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-guinea">New Guinea</a>, stressing gradual, uniform development through schools, health services and patrol posts. He later served as minister for external affairs and as Governor-General of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/australia">Australia</a> from 1969 to 1974.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/paul-hasluck.jpg" alt="Paul Hasluck" width="249" height="348" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Work of the Australian Government · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Paul_Hasluck_1971_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
